  "notes": "USAGE:\n{賑|にぎ}わう is an intransitive verb. The place that is bustling is the subject, and the people or things making it lively are marked with で ({観光客|かんこうきゃく}で{賑|にぎ}わう — bustling with tourists). It carries a positive connotation of prosperity and liveliness.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {人|ひと}で{賑|にぎ}わう: to be bustling with people\n- {観光客|かんこうきゃく}で{賑|にぎ}わう: to be bustling with tourists\n- {大|おお}いに{賑|にぎ}わう: to be very lively\n- {賑|にぎ}わいを{見|み}せる: to show liveliness\n- {賑|にぎ}わいを{取|と}り{戻|もど}す: to regain bustling activity\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{混|こ}む (to be crowded) is neutral and can be negative (uncomfortably crowded). {賑|にぎ}わう is positive, implying prosperity and cheerful energy, not just crowding. {繁盛|はんじょう}する (to prosper, to do good business) focuses on commercial success.",
